{
  "info": {
    "name": "blogplatform4 api",
    "description": "Every endpoint of the Blogging Platform IV API (Spring Security, JWT, Google OAuth2, RBAC). No tests: send the requests by hand.\n\nThe ids, usernames and bodies are real rows of blog_db:\n- user1 (id 1, password password123) is an AUTHOR. It wrote posts 603, 731 and 962, comments 2517 and 2520,\n  and review 3321. user201 (id 201) and user1000 (id 1000) are READERs.\n- Tags: 20 = linux (used), 33 = postman (unused).\n\nSetup:\n1. Start the app with an admin password, e.g.\n   $env:ADMIN_PASSWORD = \"Admin-pass1\"; ./mvnw spring-boot:run\n   The first start creates the admin account \"admin\". Use your own password in \"Log in as admin\" if it differs.\n2. Auth > Log in (user1). Copy data.accessToken from the response into the collection variable token.\n3. Auth > Log in as admin. Copy its data.accessToken into the collection variable adminToken.\n\nAuth: requests send \"Authorization: Bearer {{token}}\" (user1). Public requests send no token,\nadmin requests send {{adminToken}}. Each request's description says which roles may call it.\n\nUpdates send the version you read (0 for these rows today). After an update, the version goes up by one:\nread the row again and send the new version, or you get 409.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "adminToken",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "description": "Sign up, log in with a password or with Google, and log out.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"aline.uwase\",\n  \"email\": \"aline.uwase@amali.com\",\n  \"password\": \"secret123\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "Public: no token needed. Creates a READER. The password is stored as a BCrypt hash. username: 3-50 characters (letters, digits, . _ -); password: 8-100 characters with a letter and a digit. A second send gives 409 (username taken): change the username and email."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Log in",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"user1\",\n  \"password\": \"password123\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "Public: no token needed. Logs in user1 (AUTHOR). Returns a JWT signed with HMAC-SHA256 (claims: sub, roles, iat, exp, iss, jti). Copy data.accessToken into the token variable. 401: wrong username or password. 429: 5 failed logins for this username from this IP in 15 min."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Log in as admin",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"admin\",\n  \"password\": \"Admin-pass1\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "Public: no token needed. The password is the ADMIN_PASSWORD you started the app with. Copy data.accessToken into the adminToken variable."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Current user",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Any logged-in user (READER, AUTHOR or ADMIN). The user of the token. 401: no token, or an expired, changed or revoked one."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Log out",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "logout"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Any logged-in user (READER, AUTHOR or ADMIN). Revokes this token (in-memory blacklist): from now on it gets 401 \"revoked\". Other tokens of the same user keep working. Log in again for a new token."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Google login (open in a browser)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/oauth2/authorization/google",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "oauth2",
                "authorization",
                "google"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "Public: no token needed. Start the app with the google profile (--spring.profiles.active=google, GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET set). Open this URL in a browser, not in Postman: it redirects to Google. After the login the app saves the Google user (role READER) and answers with a JWT, as JSON or in the #access_token fragment of OAUTH2_REDIRECT_URI."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
